Interview Q&A:

Q: Why do you track both _profile and _profile_f0_median?
A: The profile (embedding) captures the overall voice characteristics. The F0 median 
   captures the fundamental frequency (pitch). Using both gives us two independent checks. 
   If the embedding is uncertain (during overlap), the pitch can serve as a tie-breaker.

Q: Why is _audio_buffer needed?
A: 20ms is too short for reliable speaker verification. We buffer 25 chunks (500ms) 
   before computing the embedding. This gives 4x improvement in embedding quality.

