5.6 _update_similarity_ema() - Detailed Explanation
What it does:

  Smooths similarity scores using Exponential Moving Average
  Prevents frame-by-frame jitter
  Gives more stable decisions


Formula:


EMA_new = α × current + (1-α) × EMA_old

Where α = 0.3 (smoothing factor)


Without smoothing:
Frame 1: 0.65 (accept)
Frame 2: 0.48 (reject)  ← Jitter!
Frame 3: 0.62 (accept)
Frame 4: 0.45 (reject)  ← Jitter!

With EMA smoothing:
Frame 1: 0.65
Frame 2: 0.60 (0.3×0.48 + 0.7×0.65)
Frame 3: 0.61 (0.3×0.62 + 0.7×0.60)
Frame 4: 0.56 (0.3×0.45 + 0.7×0.61)

Result: Stable decisions, no jitter

5.7 _detect_overlap() - Detailed Explanation

What it does:

  Detects if multiple speakers are overlapping
  Uses variance of recent similarity scores

Algorithm

def _detect_overlap(self):
    if len(recent_sims) < 5:
        return False
    
    recent = list(recent_sims)[-10:]
    variance = np.var(recent)
    
    return variance > 0.02  # High variance = overlap

Why Variance?

Single speaker:
Similarities: [0.65, 0.67, 0.64, 0.66, 0.65]
Variance: 0.0001 (low) → No overlap

Two speakers alternating:
Similarities: [0.65, 0.35, 0.62, 0.38, 0.64]
Variance: 0.015 (high) → Overlap detected!

